{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232-soooooo-what-is-it","id":232,"title":"Soooooo... What IS it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T09:52:49-07:00","id":232,"title":"Soooooo... What IS it?","content":"The Trinity Continuum seems to get a lot of people excited, but as someone who came into the hobby with the release of the new World of Darkness, I've never really had much run in with it. Can someone give me an idea what's it's all about, and why I should get pumped for new editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T10:07:21-07:00","id":240,"title":"","content":"It's a timeline- and genre-spanning <i>continuum</i> that begins with high-flying pulp adventure (<i>Adventure!), </i>continues with a semi-deconstruction superheroic epic (<i>Aberrant</i>), and ends (?) with science fiction psychics battling among the stars (<i>Aeon- </i>er<i>, Trinity). </i>Each setting is pretty much <i>stand-alone</i>, though the overarching tale, themes and (some) characters span the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Some of the <i>best </i>writing White Wolf ever printed came out of the Trinity Continuum, and I say that as a ridiculous fan of almost every property. Warren Ellis did a short story for <i>Adventure!</i> and there's a radical <i>Hunter S. Thompson</i> analog in <i>Aberrant</i>. Wonderful stuff. <i>Trinity</i> (called <i>Aeon </i>upon a time<i>) </i>still managed to be my personal favorite of the three. Totally mind-blowing science fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T10:25:38-07:00","id":263,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Continuum games were released in reverse chronological order, so it went <i>Aeon/Trinity</i> -&gt; <i>Aberrant</i> - &gt; <i>Adventure!</i>, each new game revealing some of the setting's hidden history.<br /> <br /> (If you're wondering about the <i>Aeon</i> to <i>Trinity</i> thing, White Wolf had a run-in with the makers of <i>Aeon Flux</i>. This time round, they're officially calling it <i>Trinity Continuum: Aeon</i>, which's different enough not to be seen as an infringement.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T10:53:32-07:00","id":283,"title":"","content":"Pretty much my only exposure to Trinity was with Aberrant, which was a really good &quot;new supers&quot; game. I know there were some issues with later stuff in the line, but the corebook gave a great overview of a really interesting world. I'm deeply in love with superhero games, so I'm &quot;super&quot; excited (eh? eh?) about a new edition of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T03:38:08-07:00","id":1027,"title":"","content":"All three games have appeal. And with a glance at the schedule you will see that the modern era will be first. I'm very excited and really hope that there is a kick starter project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:25:49-07:00","id":1425,"title":"","content":"I still have Adventure! on my shelf. It's pretty awesome. They knew the line was dying out when they published it and there would be no supplements, so they made it as self-contained as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/243-billionsix","name":"BillionSix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T19:49:29-07:00","id":1455,"title":"","content":"The original Aberrant book was one of the best rpg books I've ever read. (Thought so at the time anyway. Haven't read it in years.) It's hard to sell someone on because the execution<br /> of it was so much more important than it's concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T06:40:49-08:00","id":1707,"title":"","content":"One of the big things with the original AAA line was that the first HALF of each book was entirely setting fluff. It was a mix of News reports, historical documents, secret internal memos, Sports coverage, and all sorts of stuff that really got you INTO the setting of the game. Then the second half of the book was ALL crunch. All the rules, uninterrupted by 'now were're gonna have a two paragraph in character story, now we're gonna have some flavor text' sort of stuff. <br /> <br /> Not only did it make it easier (at least of me) to get into the story and the setting by having all THAT in one place as a unified continuous whole, it ALSO made it easier to find specific RULES you needed to check, because they weren't broken up by setting material, and they were laid on in a fairly logical and concise order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T08:05:44-08:00","id":1776,"title":"","content":"Agree with Tiwaz on the format of the books, although that could change with the new editions of course. <br /> <br /> I really would like PDF versions that had interactive indexes / took advantage of the full functions of PDFs to 'quick find', without having to put hundreds of my own annotations. I still find myself reaching for physical books to find things quickly, even with Trin books open on-screen, which can be a bit of a pain running G+ Hangout games (my primary gaming method these days). Those features may already be included with other newer OPP titles, but I confess that I've not bought anything 'new' since OPP took over <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T18:10:56-08:00","id":2247,"title":"","content":"I'll tell yah alittle about Each in Order of Release...<br /> <br /> TRINITY (Aeon) : Is set into the Future. Its is a Game about Psychics. Sci-Fi Setting featureing Humans, Psychics, and Aliens with Psychic Powers. These psychic powers are varied. They are written closely in the mode of Vampire Disciplines from Masquerade. Very Scrict what you can do at dots in power. Your Power trait is PSI.<br /> <br /> ABERRANT : Set at the time 10 years in the future in 2008. (now our Past) Was released in 1998. Your a NOVA (mutant) with Superpowers. What would You do with the Power of a God ? That was the catch phrase for Aberrant. Basically you had Teragen (magneto's brotherhood) vs Utopia (xavier's xmen) and a few other faction seeking to Control the Novas that are erupting. The Nova are Media Celebraties just for being a Nova. There was a Dark Conspiracy seeking to kill the Novas that noone knew anything about. Players could find out about it and seek to stop it. But Most would side with Utopia or Teragen usually. Utopia sought to use Nova to Better the World using their Powers. Teragen sought Freedom from Human Laws and Morals to do as they pleased when they pleased.<br /> <br /> ADVENTURE ! : Set in the 1920s-1930s. This is a Pulp Fiction style game. Doc Savage, Rocketeer, Buck Rogers, The Phantom, The Shadow, First Appearance Batman comics, etc... Travel the World finding Lost Worlds, Fight Crazied Manderians, Talking Apes, etc...<br /> <br /> Hope that Helps you somewhat.<br /> NOW IMHO, ABERRANT was the BEST of the Games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/589-aberrant_scion","name":"ABERRANT_SCION","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}